# The vault fixture's bytes ARE the test.
#
# app/test/fixtures/vault-sample reproduces the file shapes a mirrored Obsidian
# vault has to survive: one file ending in CRLF throughout, one ending with no
# newline byte at all, and one holding a bare `TEXT` line. mirror.test.ts asserts
# that each note's `md.text` is byte-equal to its file after a close and reopen.
#
# Git's line-ending normalisation would quietly rewrite exactly those bytes on a
# checkout where `core.autocrlf` is enabled (the Windows default), turning a
# byte-exactness test into one that passes by accident or fails for a reason
# that has nothing to do with the mirror. `-text` pins the working-tree bytes to
# the committed bytes; diffs still read as text.
app/test/fixtures/vault-sample/** -text
